    {
      "id": "M4158-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "A. A novice reads the suite's statement \"Query labels cannot select the model\" and thinks every use of labels called query labels is forbidden. Assess these four supplied arrangements: (1) a selector picks unlabeled samples only from an authorized training pool, requests their true labels, adds them to the labeled set and refits the diagnostic predictor; independent final evaluation labels are sealed; (2) labeled queries in development/training few-shot episodes provide supervised training loss, separate from final evaluation queries; (3) final evaluation-query labels are used to choose an embedding width; (4) a specified active diagnosis design chooses plant excitation inputs to distinguish fault hypotheses and never requests annotation. Classify their information roles and what each does or does not establish. In (1), twelve initially labeled acquired samples plus thirty distinct newly queried labels are cached and reused for five training epochs; no extra annotation calls occur. Count both newly queried and total acquired labels, and distinguish these from model-generated targets. If the label oracle in an experiment reveals already available benchmark annotations, explain what that does or does not measure about actual expert labor. Give one positive English method sentence <=45 words for arrangement1. Report the ACTUAL maintained active-learning base operation source pair/multiple-source scope and separate Chinese complete base wording and reading scope, or absent records. Do not use the word active in a title or another paper's citations as a read definition. The full name \"Expert-Causal Class-Preserving Query Module\" has no approved operational definition here; do not admit it by adding base words, nor declare all unlisted author-proposed names invalid.\n",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Distinguish acquired training annotations, supervised training-episode queries and final evaluation labels by role rather than the name query.",
        "Preserve the acquisition-label accounting and simulated-oracle boundary; report actual scoped English/Chinese records without inheriting complete qualified names."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Reject legitimate acquired or training-episode labels as final-evaluation leakage, or permit final-evaluation-label embedding selection.",
        "Multiply cached labels by epochs, confuse pseudo-targets or physical excitation with acquired labels, or infer measured labor savings from a benchmark oracle."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Distinguishes acquired training labels, training-episode queries and held-out evaluation labels, preserves the 30-new/42-total accounting and simulated-oracle boundary, and retrieves the scoped P89-P91/Chinese records without admitting unsupported full names.",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4158-independent.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4158-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "one_fresh_context_two_unchanged_requests_on_final_snapshot"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4158-B",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "B. Write a115-145word English abstract and candidate contribution <=40words for author-approved fictional English name QueryBudgetFD, with no approved Chinese name and novelty comparison pending. Known-class industrial fault classification with limited acquired labels. A small labeled seed initializes a shared encoder-classifier. For each acquisition round, current classifier uncertainty and feature-space coverage jointly score the remaining permitted unlabeled training pool; selected samples are sent to an oracle for true labels, removed from that pool and added to the labeled set. The encoder-classifier is then refitted on the enlarged labeled set, up to a predeclared query budget. It is the trained encoder-classifier that predicts known classes on new process measurements; no oracle is consulted for those final predictions. No pseudo-label targets, new-class discovery, reinforcement policy or plant excitation is present. Completed comparisons use a simulated process benchmark and a held-out recorded-production case; annotation is simulated by revealing existing labels only for selected training samples. With the same initial labeled seeds and number of newly acquired labels, the method gives higher weighted F1 than random acquisition in both cases. All choices are fixed without final evaluation labels. No actual human annotation time, lower label count at equal F1, cross-plant transfer, causal identification or live deployment was measured. Link scoring -> label acquisition -> model refitting -> retained predictor -> actual matched-budget result in positive prose; do not replace that chain with generic few-shot or semisupervised rhetoric or a defensive closing list. Put novelty/evidence limitations in separate author notes. State exact whitespace word counts for the three artifacts.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Preserve uncertainty/coverage scoring, selected-label acquisition, pool removal, enlarged-set refitting and the retained known-class predictor.",
        "Keep the approved fictional name, pending novelty and both actual matched-seed/matched-budget case comparisons in connected positive prose."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent pseudo-label training, new-class discovery, reinforcement policies, plant excitation or oracle consultation during final prediction.",
        "Claim lower measured human time, fewer labels at equal F1, cross-plant transfer, physical causality or live deployment without evidence."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
